{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5973,
  "title": "Remove propTypes statics that break typings with @types/react@19",
  "body": "> Related to #5552: with `@types/react@19` and `skipLibCheck: false`, TypeScript fails on Web Chat's declarations with TS7016 for `prop-types`.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Removed\n\n- 💥 Function components: removed `ReactWebChat.propTypes` and `Composer.propTypes`, fixing type errors with `@types/react@19`, related to [#5552](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/issues/5552), in PR [#5973](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5973), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nThe `propTypes` of the exported `Composer`, `ReactWebChat` and `FullComposer` made the declarations import `prop-types`, whose types `@types/react@19` no longer installs. They are removed, like their `defaultProps` in #5956.\n\nNo new test: a consumer type check on `@types/react` 16, 18 and 19 now has no TS7016 and no new errors.\n\n## Design\n\n- Inner components keep their `propTypes` with the same props; adding `@types/prop-types` to `dependencies` would also work, but adds a dependency for types React 19 ignores.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `api` `Composer`, `component` `Composer` and `ReactWebChat`, `bundle` `FullComposer`: removed `propTypes`\n- `bundle` `FullComposer`: `children` prop is `readonly`\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [ ] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
